'''''Artemisia thuscula''''' ('''Incienso''') is a species endemic to the [[Canary Islands]]. It is frequent in dry areas at lower elevations (50–700 m). Its [[Capitulum (flower)|capitula]] are globose and leaf lobes flat.<ref>{{Cite book|title=Wild flowers of the Canary Islands|last1=Bramwell|first1=David|last2=Bramwell|first2=Zoë|date=1974|publisher=Stanley Thornes|isbn=0859500101|location=London|oclc=1602895}}</ref>

